  entry
    definition "a unit of heat equal to the amount of heat required to raise the temperature of one kilogram of water by one degree at one atmosphere pressure; used by nutritionists to characterize the energy-producing potential in food"
    id oewn-13748672-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("kilogram calorie" kilocalorie "large calorie" "nutritionist's calorie")
  entry
    definition "unit of heat defined as the quantity of heat required to raise the temperature of 1 gram of water by 1 degree centigrade at atmospheric pressure"
    id oewn-13748406-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("gram calorie" "small calorie")
